Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[{
 "V2: Kay\[CloseCurlyQuote]s program do not work because of some extra \
simplifications he performs. Indeed, \[Gamma]1 followed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]2", "+"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a706db34-3b8f-644b-8712-f13fdea83675"],
 " cannot be substituted by \[Gamma]1\[Delta]\[Chi] directly: there is also \
an effective \[Gamma]g vertex\n",
 StyleBox["I wrote a new program, which works as follows:\n\ngenerate a \
string of gamma interactions from the bottom to the top of the red line. \n\
There are 4 different vertices. Note that I split Gamma_1 into the one where \
the green line goes to one, and the fluctuating part. \n\n\[Gamma]11: \
Subscript[\[CapitalGamma], 1]-vertex where the outgoing green line is set to \
1\n\[Gamma]1\[Delta]\[Chi]:  Subscript[\[CapitalGamma], 1]-vertex where the \
outgoing green line is \[Delta]\[Chi]\n\[Gamma]2p: Subsuperscript[\
\[CapitalGamma], 2, +]\n\[Gamma]2m: : Subsuperscript[\[CapitalGamma], 2, -]\n\
\nI offer all the different combinations to Mathematica. Then I count that at \
the end there are n+1 Gamma_1, and not more gamma_2 than I can \npossibly \
contract (they have \\delta \\chi fields). Whenever I see \\gamma_11 \
\\gamma_2^+, I replace by - gamma_1\\chi \n(this does the integration of \
Laplace applied to a red line). \nNote the change in the gamma_1 vertex!\n\n\
What I got at 2-loop order is in the photo I mailed. \nThere are two terms \
which are trees, and which I already threw out (boxed in the drawing). \nThen \
I find that playing at the upper right corner, there is a cancelation between \
(1)+(3), as long as we do not probe the red line. \nThe only thing which \
remains is (4). This can now be contracted in all possible ways.\n\nCan you \
check the logic of this procedure, and write a code to redo it? (I used a \
Dot[] product in Mathematica.) \n\nBoth in 1 and 2 loops, there is a single \
string which one needs then to contrast with interactions. That makes for \
some very \ndecent simplification. \n\nI succeeded to run 3 loops, 13 \
diagrams (before cancellations at the last vertex). ",
  FontSize->10]
}], "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
